# Genymotion SDK — Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A modular SDK in `/lib` with two sub-packages — **no existing code was modified**.

### File Structure

```
lib/
├── tsconfig.json
├── backend/
│   ├── index.ts              ← Barrel exports + GenymotionSDK factory
│   ├── types.ts              ← All shared types
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── EmulatorProvider.ts   ← Provider interface (swap point)
│   │   └── InstanceManager.ts    ← Orchestration layer (DI)
│   ├── providers/
│   │   └── GenymotionProvider.ts  ← Genymotion SaaS REST implementation
│   ├── auth/
│   │   └── AuthManager.ts        ← JWT + API-token with auto-refresh
│   ├── transport/
│   │   └── HttpClient.ts         ← IHttpClient interface + Axios adapter
│   └── utils/
│       ├── RetryPolicy.ts        ← Exponential backoff with jitter
│       └── Logger.ts             ← Console + Silent loggers
└── react-sdk/
    ├── index.ts              ← Barrel exports
    ├── types.ts              ← GenyDeviceProps, GenyDeviceRef, ConnectionState
    ├── genymotion.d.ts       ← Type declaration for device-web-player
    ├── GenyDevice.tsx        ← Stream-only component (forwardRef)
    ├── useGenyConnection.ts  ← WebRTC lifecycle hook (SSR-safe)
    └── useDeviceStream.ts    ← Credential resolution hook
```

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Backend SDK"
        IM["InstanceManager"] --> EP["EmulatorProvider interface"]
        EP --> GP["GenymotionProvider"]
        EP --> CP["CustomProvider (yours)"]
        GP --> AM["AuthManager"]
        GP --> HC["HttpClient (Axios)"]
        GP --> RP["RetryPolicy"]
    end

    subgraph "React SDK"
        GD["GenyDevice"] --> UGC["useGenyConnection"]
        GD --> UDS["useDeviceStream"]
        UGC --> DWP["@genymotion/device-web-player"]
    end

    GD -.-> |"getStreamUrl()"| IM
```

---

## Usage Examples

### 1. Backend — Quick Start (API Token)

```ts
import { GenymotionSDK } from './lib/backend';

const sdk = new GenymotionSDK({
  auth: { type: 'api-token', apiToken: process.env.GENYMOTION_API_KEY! },
  logLevel: 'debug',
});

// Create + wait for ONLINE + get stream credentials
const { instance, stream } = await sdk.instanceManager.createAndWait({
  recipeUuid: 'your-recipe-uuid',
  name: 'test-device-1',
});

console.log(stream.webrtcUrl, stream.token);

// Later: stop
await sdk.instanceManager.stopInstance(instance.uuid);
```

### 2. Backend — JWT Authentication

```ts
import { GenymotionSDK } from './lib/backend';

const sdk = new GenymotionSDK({
  auth: { type: 'jwt', email: 'you@example.com', password: 'secret' },
});
// JWT auto-refreshes before expiry — no manual token management needed
```

### 3. Backend — Individual Module Imports

```ts
import { AuthManager } from './lib/backend/auth/AuthManager';
import { AxiosHttpClient } from './lib/backend/transport/HttpClient';
import { GenymotionProvider } from './lib/backend/providers/GenymotionProvider';
import { InstanceManager } from './lib/backend/core/InstanceManager';
import { ConsoleLogger } from './lib/backend/utils/Logger';

const logger = new ConsoleLogger('debug');
const httpClient = new AxiosHttpClient({ logger });
const authManager = new AuthManager({
  credentials: { type: 'api-token', apiToken: 'your-token' },
  httpClient,
  logger,
});

const provider = new GenymotionProvider({ httpClient, authManager, logger });
const manager = new InstanceManager(provider, logger);
```

### 4. React — GenyDevice Component

```tsx
import { GenyDevice } from './lib/react-sdk';

// Auto-connect via instanceId
<GenyDevice
  instanceId="abc-123"
  apiKey="your-api-token"
  autoConnect
  style={{ width: 400, height: 800 }}
/>

// Direct stream URL
<GenyDevice streamUrl="wss://..." token="access-token" autoConnect />
```

### 5. React — Imperative Control via Ref

```tsx
import { useRef } from 'react';
import { GenyDevice, type GenyDeviceRef } from './lib/react-sdk';

function Player() {
  const ref = useRef<GenyDeviceRef>(null);

  return (
    <>
      <GenyDevice ref={ref} instanceId="abc-123" apiKey="token" />
      <button onClick={() => ref.current?.connect()}>Connect</button>
      <button onClick={() => ref.current?.disconnect()}>Disconnect</button>
      <button onClick={() => ref.current?.reload()}>Reload</button>
      <button onClick={() => console.log(ref.current?.getStatus())}>Status</button>
    </>
  );
}
```

### 6. Replace Genymotion with Another Provider

```ts
import type { EmulatorProvider } from './lib/backend/core/EmulatorProvider';
import { InstanceManager } from './lib/backend/core/InstanceManager';

class AWSDeviceFarmProvider implements EmulatorProvider {
  async createInstance(config) { /* AWS Device Farm API */ }
  async startInstance(id) { /* ... */ }
  async stopInstance(id) { /* ... */ }
  async deleteInstance(id) { /* ... */ }
  async getInstanceStatus(id) { /* ... */ }
  async waitUntilReady(id, timeout?) { /* ... */ }
  async createSnapshot(id, config) { /* ... */ }
  async restoreSnapshot(recipeId, name) { /* ... */ }
  async connectAdb(id) { /* ... */ }
  async getStreamUrl(id) { /* ... */ }
  async listRecipes() { /* ... */ }
  async listInstances() { /* ... */ }
}

// Inject your provider — frontend code doesn't change at all
const manager = new InstanceManager(new AWSDeviceFarmProvider());
```

### 7. CI — GitHub Actions

```yaml
name: Android E2E Tests
on: [push]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: 20 }
      - run: npm ci

      - name: Start Genymotion Instance
        env:
          GENY_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GENYMOTION_API_KEY }}
        run: |
          node -e "
            const { GenymotionSDK } = require('./lib/backend');
            const sdk = new GenymotionSDK({
              auth: { type: 'api-token', apiToken: process.env.GENY_API_TOKEN }
            });
            sdk.instanceManager.createAndWait({
              recipeUuid: '${{ vars.RECIPE_UUID }}',
              name: 'ci-\${{ github.run_id }}'
            }).then(({ instance }) => {
              console.log('INSTANCE_ID=' + instance.uuid);
            });
          "

      - name: Run Tests
        run: npm test

      - name: Cleanup
        if: always()
        run: |
          node -e "
            const { GenymotionSDK } = require('./lib/backend');
            const sdk = new GenymotionSDK({
              auth: { type: 'api-token', apiToken: process.env.GENY_API_TOKEN }
            });
            sdk.instanceManager.stopInstance(process.env.INSTANCE_ID);
          "
```

---

## Error Handling Strategy

| Layer | Strategy |
|---|---|
| `RetryPolicy` | Auto-retries 5xx, 429, network errors with exponential backoff + jitter |
| `AuthManager` | Auto-refreshes JWT 1h before 48h expiry |
| `GenymotionProvider` | All API calls wrapped in retry; `waitUntilReady()` throws on terminal states |
| `GenyDevice` | `onError` callback; `data-geny-status` attribute for CSS-based state indication |

